"""Kaggle runner: sealed 18d OOS generative-return FINAL eval — cosine pilot Seg9 + Seg0.

One-shot final evaluation (NOT a tuning loop) of the C1 forecast cosine pilot's
val-gen-IC-best snapshot ``pilot_seg009`` alongside its parent
``seg000_beta_v21_release_best475`` (Beta v2.1 release Best@475), on the sealed
package ``kronos_beta_v2_time_oos_through_20260903`` (18 dates / 92,751 windows).

Contract = Baseline 2 (``evaluate_beta_v21_generative_return_oos``), prod arm only:
T=0.65 / top_p=0.8 / N=5 / seed 20260906; score = mean_N AR samples of
``denorm_close_d10 / last_close - 1``; zero training.

Robustness (lessons from earlier OOS kernels):
- Seg9 first, then Seg0: workers claim (checkpoint, arm, date) tasks dynamically
  in plan order, so every Seg9 shard is taken before any Seg0 shard.
- Every date shard is written the moment it finishes (``shards/``) and scored by
  the parent on the next poll (``results/progress.json`` + SwanLab + run.log).
- Each checkpoint is scored and saved (summary, predictions, per-date CSV,
  comparison.json) as soon as its 18th shard lands; a 12h kill cannot take a
  finished checkpoint with it.
"""

